Withings added one accessor to tasks.c, at 0x73634 in appl v3411: it hands back a
task's stack bounds, with the usual "NULL handle means the running task" rule.
It sits immediately after uxTaskGetStackHighWaterMark in the image, so it goes
there here too. The image's body is six instructions -- no assert, no critical
section -- storing pxEndOfStack through the first pointer and pxStack through
the second. The SDK's sources are CRLF, so this patch is too.

--- a/tasks.c
+++ b/tasks.c
@@ -3671,6 +3671,17 @@
 #endif /* INCLUDE_uxTaskGetStackHighWaterMark */
 /*-----------------------------------------------------------*/
 
+void vTaskGetStackBounds( TaskHandle_t xTask, StackType_t **ppxEndOfStack, StackType_t **ppxStack )
+{
+TCB_t *pxTCB;
+
+	pxTCB = prvGetTCBFromHandle( xTask );
+
+	*ppxEndOfStack = pxTCB->pxEndOfStack;
+	*ppxStack = pxTCB->pxStack;
+}
+/*-----------------------------------------------------------*/
+
 #if ( INCLUDE_vTaskDelete == 1 )
 
 	static void prvDeleteTCB( TCB_t *pxTCB )
